[{"explanation":{"text":["Here, S = {1, 2, 3, 4, ...., 19, 20}","Let E = event of getting a multiple of 3 or 5","= {3, 6 , 9, 12, 15, 18, 5, 10, 20}","∴P(E)=$\\frac{n(E)}{n(S)}$=$\\frac{9}{20}$"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e158ac0b9bf207ccab187f","text":["Tickets numbered 1 to 20 are mixed up and then a ticket is drawn at random. What is the probability that the ticket drawn has a number which is a multiple of 3 or 5?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","image":"","_id":"65e158ac0b9bf207ccab1880"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","image":"","_id":"65e158ac0b9bf207ccab1881"},{"text":"$\\frac{8}{15}$","image":"","_id":"65e158ac0b9bf207ccab1882"},{"text":"$\\frac{9}{20}$","image":"","_id":"65e158ac0b9bf207ccab1883"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:25:16.393Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:25:16.393Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Getting at most Two heads means 0 to 2 but not more than 2","Here S = {TTT, TTH, THT, HTT, THH, HTH, HHT, HHH}","Let E = event of getting at most two heads","Then E = {TTT, TTH, THT, HTT, THH, HTH, HHT}","∴P(E)=$\\frac{n(E)}{n(S)}$ = $\\frac{7}{8}$"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e15ab50b9bf207ccab189f","text":["Three unbiased coins are tossed. What is the probability of getting at most two heads?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","image":"","_id":"65e15ab50b9bf207ccab18a0"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{4}$","image":"","_id":"65e15ab50b9bf207ccab18a1"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{8}$","image":"","_id":"65e15ab50b9bf207ccab18a2"},{"text":"$\\frac{7}{8}$","image":"","_id":"65e15ab50b9bf207ccab18a3"}],"correctOptionIndex":4,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:33:57.194Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:33:57.194Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In two throws of a dice, n(S) = (6 x 6) = 36","Let E = event of getting a sum","= {(3, 6), (4, 5), (5, 4), (6, 3)}","∴P(E)=$\\frac{n(E)}{n(S)}$","$\\frac{4}{36}$ = $\\frac{1}{9}$"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e15a450b9bf207ccab1899","text":["What is the probability of getting a sum 9 from two throws of a dice?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{6}$","image":"","_id":"65e15a450b9bf207ccab189a"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{8}$","image":"","_id":"65e15a450b9bf207ccab189b"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{9}$","image":"","_id":"65e15a450b9bf207ccab189c"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{12}$","image":"","_id":"65e15a450b9bf207ccab189d"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:32:05.271Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:32:05.271Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Total number of balls","= (8 + 7 + 6)","= 21","Let E = event that the ball drawn is neither red nor green","= event that the ball drawn is blue","∴n(E)=7∴P(E)=n(E)n(S)=13$\\frac{7}{21}$ = $\\frac{1}{3}$"],"images":[]},"_id":"65e159580b9bf207ccab188a","text":["In a box, there are 8 red, 7 blue and 6 green balls. One ball is picked up randomly. What is the probability that it is neither red nor green?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{3}$","image":"","_id":"65e159580b9bf207ccab188b"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","image":"","_id":"65e159580b9bf207ccab188c"},{"text":"$\\frac{7}{19}$","image":"","_id":"65e159580b9bf207ccab188d"},{"text":"$\\frac{8}{21}$","image":"","_id":"65e159580b9bf207ccab188e"}],"correctOptionIndex":1,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:28:08.910Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:28:08.910Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["In a simultaneous throw of two dice, we have n(S) = (6 x 6) = 36","Then, E = {(1, 2), (1, 4), (1, 6), (2, 1), (2, 2), (2, 3), (2, 4), (2, 5), (2, 6), (3, 2), (3, 4), (3, 6), (4, 1), (4, 2), (4, 3), (4, 4), (4, 5), (4, 6), (5, 2), (5, 4), (5, 6), (6, 1), (6, 2), (6, 3), (6, 4), (6, 5), (6, 6)}","∴n(E)=27","∴P(E)=$\\frac{n(E)}{n(S)}$ = $\\frac{27}{36}$ = $\\frac{3}{4}$ "],"images":[]},"_id":"65e15b320b9bf207ccab18bd","text":["Two dice are thrown simultaneously. What is the probability of getting two numbers whose product is even?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","image":"","_id":"65e15b320b9bf207ccab18be"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{4}$","image":"","_id":"65e15b320b9bf207ccab18bf"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{8}$","image":"","_id":"65e15b320b9bf207ccab18c0"},{"text":"$\\frac{5}{16}$","image":"","_id":"65e15b320b9bf207ccab18c1"}],"correctOptionIndex":2,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:36:02.514Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:36:02.514Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["Here, n(S) = 52","Let E = event of getting a queen of club or a king of heart","Then, n(E) = 2","∴P(E)=$\\frac{n(E)}{n(S)}$","= $\\frac{2}{52}$ ","= $\\frac{1}{26}$ "],"images":[]},"_id":"65e15cd20b9bf207ccab192b","text":["A card is drawn from a pack of 52 cards. The probability of getting a queen of club or a king of heart is:"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{13}$","image":"","_id":"65e15cd20b9bf207ccab192c"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{13}$","image":"","_id":"65e15cd20b9bf207ccab192d"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{26}$","image":"","_id":"65e15cd20b9bf207ccab192e"},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{52}$","image":"","_id":"65e15cd20b9bf207ccab192f"}],"correctOptionIndex":3,"difficulty":"L1","topic":"probability","subTopic":"subtopic1","entrance_exams":[],"createdAt":"2024-03-01T04:42:58.960Z","updatedAt":"2024-03-01T04:42:58.960Z","__v":0},{"explanation":{"text":["P(getting a prize)","= $\\frac{10}{10+25}$","= $\\frac{10}{35}$ ","= $\\frac{2}{7}$ "],"images":[]},"_id":"65e15c0a0b9bf207ccab18fc","text":["In a lottery, there are 10 prizes and 25 blanks. A lottery is drawn at random. What is the probability of getting a prize?"],"images":[],"options":[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{10}$","image":"","_id":"65e15c0a0b9bf207ccab18fd"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","image":"","_id":"65e15c0a0b9bf207ccab18fe"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{7}$","image"